cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PreWarp, please cite it as below, and cite the NIST AM-Bench data it was validated on."
title: "PreWarp: inherent-strain distortion prediction and compensation for metal LPBF parts"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Albert
    family-names: Salsench Virgili
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sals121/prewarp"
url: "https://github.com/sals121/prewarp"
abstract: >-
  Predicts and pre-compensates the distortion of metal laser powder bed fusion (LPBF/SLM) parts
  with an inherent-strain finite element model, validated against the NIST AM-Bench 2018 and 2022
  bridge measurements, with an MCP server and a Claude agent on top.
keywords:
  - additive manufacturing
  - LPBF
  - distortion
  - inherent strain
  - finite element method
  - NIST AM-Bench
